WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.369 line:0%
-We're talking about cascading
system-wide effects, Ian.

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.171 line:0%
-Gosh, that's a drag.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.307 line:0%
-What is the matter with you?
-Drag?

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.542 line:0%
-Why? Is there something special
you wanted me to do?

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.177
-How about give a damn?
-Far too much not to care.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:15.248
-Hey. I gave my opinion robustly
for years.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.484
As expected,
the sum of our human endeavors

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.152
has led to our annihilation.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:22.255
And the only play now is to take
the time that we have left

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:25.825
and, uh, you know, just like
we always do, squander it.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.094
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.762
That was a clip from
"Jurassic World: Dominion."

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.163
We're here with Jeff Goldblum.

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:32.865
And your friends.

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:36.736
-Well, yes, yes. How about that?
Don't they look great?

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.604
The great Sam Neill

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.940
and the great Oscar-winning
Laura Dern, of course.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.308
-You have all --

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.276
All three of you
have aged fantastically well.

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:45.678
-I don't know about me.
They have.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.014
They look like supermodels.
-And this is the first time

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.850
you guys have worked together,
all three of you, since 1993.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.153
-Not been reunited on screen or
anyplace else professionally,

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.621
you know, all this time.

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:57.923
I adore them, you know,
and they've changed my life.

00:00:57.923 --> 00:01:00.060
They're so wonderful.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.496
But what was I gonna say?
Wait a minute.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.331
-The three of you together...
-Oh, the three of us together!

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.567
Yes, yes, and we're not --

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.702
We're not -- That isn't
all of us in the movie.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.137
-Yeah.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.973
-We are liberally distributed

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.676
throughout the movie,
if anybody's interested.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.811
And you want to go see it
this weekend, don't you?

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.179
-Yeah, opening weekend.
-Before all your friends...

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:21.547
-Before anybody
ruins it for you.

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:22.748
-Yes. Yes.

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:24.550
And you want to see it
on the big screen.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:25.951
-You do.

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:27.887
And, now, one thing that --
You all look the same,

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.089
but obviously technology
has changed a great deal.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.691
This was an incredibly
technologically advanced film

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:34.160
in 1993.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.063
More CGI now. Still some
animatronic stuff, yes?

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.799
-You know, originally,
I've been --

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.167
I've come to realize recently

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.536
it was a game-changing
technological intersection

00:01:44.536 --> 00:01:47.173
with our movie in bringing
those dinosaurs to life.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.409
Dennis Muren was, you know --

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.945
What was it called? ILM and CGI.

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:55.915
And -- And so --
And people have said

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:59.018
it's like when sound
was introduced into movies.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.987
I never realized that,
but I guess over the last

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.989
couple of decades,
it really has changed things.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.124
Now, in this movie,
Colin Trevorrow,

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.694
our wonderful director,
had a vision and an idea

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:10.262
that mostly
they would be not tennis balls

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:12.665
and painted in later
that we were looking at,

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.633
but animatronics.
-Wow!

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:16.669
-So it's a whole array
and a bigger array

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:20.973
of dinosaurs actually made,
that were there with us,

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:22.275
than you've ever seen.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.675
That's what we mostly
did it with this time.

00:02:23.675 --> 00:02:26.312
-You -- Obviously you have been
in the kind of films

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.581
where there will be merchandise
with your face on it,

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.450
but I have heard.
and you brought some examples,

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.185
that you're most excited

00:02:33.185 --> 00:02:36.322
when people have actually
received a Jeff Goldblum tattoo.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:39.191
-Well, I get excited
here and there, yeah.

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:40.693
-I mean -- And I guess

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.028
they've gone out of their way
to show you.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.529
If they're gonna get it,
they're gonna show you.

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:45.064
-Sometimes that's true.
-There you go.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:46.199
There's "Life Finds a Way."

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:49.469
There you are
coming out of an egg.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.603 line:0%
This --
I mean, that's really great.

00:02:51.603 --> 00:02:54.673 line:0%
-Hey. Some of these artists...
-They're really good.

00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:58.177 line:0%
This is -- I like --
Just this request is a fun one.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.845
-I've never seen that one.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.747
Me as the spitter.
-Yeah.

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:05.284
-I can get a little bit juicy
sometimes. That's true.

00:03:05.284 --> 00:03:07.753
-But this -- I mean, the iconic

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:10.823
"Jurassic Park" sex symbol
right there.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.426
Yeah, yeah, I love that.
Well, you enjoy it.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.861
You enjoy it. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:19.365
-You're also doing, uh --

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.300
You're reprising your role
as Grandmaster in "Thor,"

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.535
which is such a fun part,

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.169
and I'm very happy
you're doing that again.

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:25.171
-Thank you very much.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.539
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.908
-I'm looking forward to it.
-Well, thank you.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:31.210
The -- I, uh -- This has --

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.546
You brought it up.
So it hasn't been publicly --

00:03:34.546 --> 00:03:36.282
Seth, let me say this.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.550
-Are you not?

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.351
Have we not publicly said
you're in it?

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:43.022
-[ Stammers ]

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.824
Let me say this.
-Okay.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:49.895
-I think it's my greatest
theatrical appearance.

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:52.999
You -- You never
physically see me on screen.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.267
-Wow.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.568
-You don't hear an utterance
that I ever make.

00:03:56.568 --> 00:03:59.205
And I'm never referred to

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:01.940
by any other character
in the movie.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.076
But in many, many scenes,

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:07.313
the sensitive viewer

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.249
will feel my vibrations
all throughout.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:12.252
-That's great.
-I could only have attempted

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.853
this this year --
I don't think before.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:16.555
-Wow. That's great. Well, based
on what you said about it,

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:19.258
I'm happy to announce
I'm in it, too?

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:22.294
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:24.530
Hey. Thank you for being here.
Oh. You're gonna stick around.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.866
We're gonna keep you here.
You guys, that's Jeff Goldblum.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.835
"Jurassic World: Dominion" is
in theaters and IMAX tomorrow.

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:32.238
We'll be right back
with D'Arcy Carden, everybody.

